## Parameter ownership

Each write sends the complete planned `parameters` object. A successful write removes omitted keys; Contentful can reject the request if a required parameter is missing. Omitting the entire object can clear existing values. Changing an ordinary parameter also resubmits the planned secrets, which can overwrite external rotations that refresh could not detect.

Changing only `timeouts` updates Terraform state without writing the installation. Changing `marketplace` acknowledgments still writes the complete planned parameter object.

When Contentful returns an all-asterisk value, the provider can preserve the corresponding value from the plan or prior state. A preserved value does not verify the current remote secret. Import retains returned masks because the original values are unavailable. See [App Installation secrets](../guides/secrets-and-state#app-installation-secrets) for rotation, import, and changes outside Terraform.

